LICENSE AGREEMENT

Last Updated: November 19, 2026

THIS LICENSE AGREEMENT (THIS “AGREEMENT”) IS A BINDING CONTRACT BETWEEN DOPPEL
INC., A DELAWARE CORPORATION (“DOPPEL”), AND THE INDIVIDUAL, COMPANY OR OTHER
ENTITY THAT DOWNLOADS OR USES THE FEED (“RECIPIENT”). BY DOWNLOADING OR USING
THE FEED, RECIPIENT AGREES TO THIS AGREEMENT, AND ANY INDIVIDUAL DOING SO ON
BEHALF OF AN ENTITY REPRESENTS THAT HE OR SHE IS AUTHORIZED TO BIND IT. IF
RECIPIENT DOES NOT AGREE, OR DOES NOT HAVE SUCH AUTHORITY, IT MUST NOT DOWNLOAD,
ACCESS OR USE THE FEED.

THE FEED IS FREE AND PROVIDED “AS IS.” SECTIONS 5 AND 6 SIGNIFICANTLY LIMIT
DOPPEL’S RESPONSIBILITY TO RECIPIENT.

1. The Feed

1.1 Feed. The “Feed” is the threat intelligence feed Doppel makes available
    through its public GitHub repository at
    https://github.com/doppelxyz/secr-intel or any alternative location (the
    “Repository”). It includes the intelligence threat data and indicators of
    malicious activity in the feed, such as domains, URLs, and IP addresses,
    together with related metadata (“Feed Data”), and all related documentation
    and source notices. “Use” of the Feed includes downloading, copying,
    storing, and processing it.

1.2 Updates. Doppel may update the Feed from time to time but is not required to
    do so. Any update is part of the Feed.

2. Permitted Use

2.1 License. Subject to this Agreement, Doppel grants Recipient a limited,
    non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable, royalty-free
    license to use the Feed solely for Recipient’s internal defensive
    cybersecurity purposes (the “Permitted Purpose”), which consists of:

    (a) creating and implementing internal security rules, configurations,
        alerts, detections, blocking decisions, risk determinations, and other
        defensive measures (“Defensive Measures”) to protect the systems,
        networks, personnel, and data of Recipient and its related entities that
        control, are controlled by, or are under common control with Recipient
        (“Affiliates”); and

    (b) loading the Feed into Recipient’s own security tools (such as SIEM,
        SOAR, firewall, IDS/IPS, endpoint, and DNS security tools) for that
        purpose.

2.2 Affiliates and Service Providers. An Affiliate or contractor of Client
    providing security services to Recipient or its Affiliates (“Service
    Providers”) may use the Feed for the Permitted Purpose on Recipient’s
    behalf, provided such Service Provider is bound by written terms at least as
    protective of the Feed as this Agreement and doesn’t use the Feed for its
    own benefit or for the benefit of any other customer (except to pursuant to
    its own written license obtained from Doppel). Recipient is responsible for
    their compliance. Use by Service Providers under this Section is not a
    disclosure to a third party in violation of this Agreement.

2.3 No Other Use. Any use of the Feed or Feed Data not specified herein is
    prohibited, including any offensive or “hack back” activity against systems
    or persons identified in the Feed.

3. Attribution

3.1 Source Notices. Recipient must keep any attribution, proprietary,
    disclaimer, or source notice included with the Feed, including any
    attribution statement specified in the Repository (“Attribution Notice”) in
    all copies of Feed Data, including within security tools to the extent
    technically possible.

3.2 Attribution to Doppel. Whenever Feed Data is shown to any user (for example,
    in a dashboard, alert, or report), Recipient must, to the extent technically
    possible, clearly identify Doppel as the source, using the Attribution
    Notice in the Repository or, if none, the statement “Source: Doppel Threat
    Intelligence Feed.”

3.3 No Endorsement. Recipient must not suggest that Doppel endorses or is
    affiliated with Recipient or its products or services, or use Doppel’s name
    or marks except for the attribution required above.

4. Restrictions

4.1 Prohibited Actions. Except as permitted in Section 2 or 4.2, Recipient must
    not, and must not allow others to:

    (a) sell, license, or otherwise commercialize the Feed or a substantial part
        of it, whether taken at once or over time, or any part from which a
        substantial part of the Feed could be reconstructed (“Material Portion”)

    (b) repackage the Feed or a Material Portion of it as part of any product,
        service, or feed offered to others, whether or not for a fee;

    (c) include Feed Data in, or use it to build, populate, enrich, improve or
        validate any separate database, dataset, or feed, that is made available
        to others or used for commercial purposes outside the Permitted Purpose;

    (d) input the Feed Data into or use it to develop, train, tune, fine tune,
        refine, improve or evaluate any machine learning or other artificial
        intelligence technology or model that is made available to others or
        used for commercial purposes outside the Permitted Purpose;

    (e) share or disclose the Feed or a Material Portion of it with any third
        party, including by posting it publicly or to any repository or sharing
        platform;

    (f) remove, circumvent or alter any Attribution Notice or misrepresent the
        source of Feed Data; or

    (g) use the Feed or Feed Data in violation of law or to build, improve or
        offer any product or service that competes with Doppel.

4.2 Defensive Measures Allowed. Nothing in this Agreement prevents Recipient
    from using the Feed to create and implement Defensive Measures in accordance
    with Section 2.1, as long as Recipient does not disclose or share the Feed
    or a Material Portion of it with any third party in doing so. Incidental
    disclosure of individual indicators in the normal operation of a Defensive
    Measure (for example, a block page naming a blocked domain) is permitted.

4.3 Legally Required Disclosure. Recipient may disclose Feed Data to the extent
    required by law or court order, after giving Doppel prompt notice where
    legally permitted and disclosing only the minimum Feed Data legally
    required.

5. Disclaimer of Warranties

5.1 Nature of the Feed. Recipient acknowledges that threat intelligence is
    time-sensitive and imperfect. Indicators may become outdated or benign, and
    Doppel’s review before each release does not guarantee that any Feed Data is
    accurate, complete, current, or free of false positives or false negatives.
    Recipient is solely responsible for independently evaluating Feed Data and
    for its own Defensive Measures and decisions.

5.2 DISCLAIMER. THE FEED IS PROVIDED “AS IS,” “AS AVAILABLE” AND “WITH ALL
    FAULTS.” TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, DOPPEL EXPRESSLY DISCLAIMS
    ALL WARRANTIES, EXPRESS, IMPLIED, OR STATUTORY, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF
    MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT,
    ACCURACY, AND COMPLETENESS, AND ANY WARRANTIES ARISING FROM COURSE OF
    DEALING, COURSE OF PERFORMANCE, OR USAGE OF TRADE. DOPPEL DOES NOT WARRANT
    THAT THE FEED WILL BE ACCURATE, COMPLETE, CURRENT, OR FREE OF ERRORS OR
    FALSE POSITIVES, THAT IT WILL IDENTIFY ANY PARTICULAR THREAT, THAT ANY
    DEFENSIVE MEASURE BASED ON IT WILL PREVENT ANY SECURITY INCIDENT, OR THAT
    ITS USE WILL NOT DISRUPT LEGITIMATE ACTIVITY.

5.3 NO DUTY TO UPDATE. DOPPEL HAS NO OBLIGATION TO UPDATE, CORRECT, OR MAINTAIN
    THE FEED, TO REMOVE ANY INDICATOR THAT HAS BECOME INACCURATE OR BENIGN, OR
    TO NOTIFY RECIPIENT OF ANY ERROR OR CHANGE. Any person who believes an
    indicator in the Feed has been listed in error may submit a request for
    review to secr@doppel.com with supporting information. Doppel shall have no
    obligation to respond to any such request, but may, without limiting
    anything in this Section, consider such request and may, in its sole
    discretion, remove or modify any indicator.

5.4 THIRD-PARTY PLATFORMS. DOPPEL IS NOT RESPONSIBLE FOR GITHUB OR ANY OTHER
    PLATFORM HOSTING THE REPOSITORY OR FOR ANY INCOMPATIBILITY OF THE FEED WITH
    ANY SECURITY TOOL

6. Limitation of Liability

6.1 NO LIABILITY FOR USE OR RELIANCE. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW,
    RECIPIENT ASSUMES ALL RISK OF USING OR RELYING ON THE FEED, AND DOPPEL HAS
    NO LIABILITY FOR ANY LOSS ARISING FROM (A) ANY SECURITY INCIDENT OR BREACH;
    (B) THE FAILURE OR INEFFECTIVENESS OF ANY DEFENSIVE MEASURE OR SECURITY
    TOOL; (C) ANY ACTION TAKEN OR NOT TAKEN BASED ON THE FEED, INCLUDING
    BLOCKING LEGITIMATE ACTIVITY OR ANY CLAIM BY A PERSON WHOSE DOMAIN OR IP
    ADDRESS APPEARS IN THE FEED; OR (D) ANY ERROR IN, OR FAILURE TO UPDATE, THE
    FEED.

6.2 EXCLUDED DAMAGES. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, DOPPEL AND ITS
    AFFILIATES, PERSONNEL, AND LICENSORS (THE “DOPPEL PARTIES”) WILL NOT BE
    LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE
    DAMAGES, OR FOR LOST PROFITS, LOST DATA, BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, OR INCIDENT
    RESPONSE COSTS ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THIS AGREEMENT OR THE FEED,
    UNDER ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THEIR POSSIBILITY AND EVEN
    IF ANY LIMITED REMEDY FAILS OF ITS ESSENTIAL PURPOSE.

6.3 CAP. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE DOPPEL PARTIES WILL HAVE NO
    LIABILITY OF ANY KIND ARISING FROM THIS AGREEMENT OR THE FEED, UNDER ANY
    THEORY. IF, DESPITE THE FOREGOING, A DOPPEL PARTY IS FOUND LIABLE, THE
    DOPPEL PARTIES' TOTAL LIABILITY TO RECIPIENT AND ITS AFFILIATES, FOR ALL
    CLAIMS COMBINED, WILL NOT EXCEED US$100.

6.4 Basis of the Bargain. Recipient acknowledges that Doppel makes the Feed
    available free of charge, that the disclaimers in Section 5 and the
    limitations in this Section 6 are an essential basis of the bargain between
    the parties, and that Doppel would not make the Feed available without them.

7. Recipient Responsibility; Indemnity

7.1 Responsibility. Recipient is solely responsible for its use of the Feed, for
    the configuration and operation of its security tools and Defensive
    Measures, and for complying with applicable laws, including export control
    and sanctions laws.

7.2 Indemnity. Recipient will defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the Doppel
    Parties from any third-party claim, and related losses, damages,
    liabilities, and costs (including reasonable attorneys’ fees), arising from
    Recipient’s or its Affiliates’ or Service Providers’ use of the Feed
    (including any Defensive Measure or other action taken based on the Feed) or
    breach of this Agreement.

8. Ownership

8.1 Doppel’s Rights. As between the parties, Doppel and its licensors own the
    Feed, including any rights in its selection and arrangement of Feed Data and
    other intellectual property rights in the Feed and Feed Data. Except for the
    limited license in Section 2, this Agreement grants Recipient no rights in
    the Feed or Feed Data in any Doppel intellectual property, and Doppel
    reserves all other rights. Publishing the Feed in a public repository does
    not place it in the public domain or under any open-source license that
    applies to other content in the Repository.

8.2 Feedback. If Recipient provides Doppel with any suggestions, comments,
    false-positive reports, or other feedback regarding the Feed (“Feedback”),
    Doppel may use such Feedback for any purpose without restriction or
    obligation to Recipient.

9. Changes and Termination

9.1 Changes to the Feed. Doppel may change, suspend, or discontinue the Feed at
    any time, with or without notice and without liability.

9.2 Termination. This Agreement starts when Recipient first downloads or uses
    the Feed. Recipient may end it by stopping all use of the Feed. Doppel may
    terminate it at any time by notice (including by posting in the Repository)
    or by discontinuing the Feed. The Agreement ends automatically if Recipient
    breaches Section 2, 3, or 4.

9.3 Effect of Termination. On termination, Recipient must stop using the Feed
    and delete all copies of Feed Data, except copies in routine backups (which
    remain subject to this Agreement until deleted) and Defensive Measures
    already in place that do not contain a Material Portion of the Feed.
    Sections 4 through 8, this Section 9.3, and Section 10 survive termination.

10. General

10.1 Changes to this Agreement. Doppel may update this Agreement by posting a
     new version in the Repository with a new “Last Updated” date. Continued use
     of the Feed after posting means Recipient accepts the updated version. If
     Recipient does not agree to the revised terms, Recipient must cease using
     the Feed.

10.2 Governing Law. This Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of
     California, excluding its conflict-of-laws rules. The UN Convention on
     Contracts for the International Sale of Goods does not apply. Each party
     irrevocably submits to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal
     courts located in Orange County, California for any dispute arising out of
     or relating to this Agreement, the Feed or Feed Data, and waives any
     objection to venue in such courts.

10.3 Injunctive Relief. Recipient acknowledges that any breach of Section 3,
     Section 4, or Section 8 may cause Doppel irreparable harm for which
     monetary damages would be inadequate, and that Doppel is entitled to seek
     injunctive or other equitable relief to prevent or remedy any such breach,
     without the necessity of posting a bond or proving actual damages, in
     addition to any other remedies available at law or in equity, in any court
     of competent jurisdiction.

10.4 Relationship. The parties are independent contractors. This Agreement
     creates no partnership, joint venture, fiduciary, franchise, or agency
     relationship.

10.5 Assignment. Recipient may not assign or transfer this Agreement or any of
     its rights or obligations hereunder, whether by operation of law, change of
     control, merger, or otherwise, without Doppel’s prior written consent, and
     any attempted assignment or transfer in violation of this Section 10.5 is
     void. Doppel may freely assign this Agreement. This Agreement binds and
     benefits the parties and their respective permitted successors and assigns.

10.6 Notices. Doppel may give notice by posting in the Repository or by email or
     other contact point provided by Recipient. Recipient must send notices to
     legal@doppel.com.

10.7 Other Terms. No failure or delay by Doppel in exercising any right under
     this Agreement operates as a waiver of that right. If any provision of this
     Agreement is held invalid or unenforceable, that provision will be enforced
     to the maximum extent permissible and the remaining provisions will remain
     in full force and effect. This Agreement is the entire agreement regarding
     the Feed, unless Doppel and Recipient sign a separate agreement that
     expressly covers the Feed, which will control in case of conflict. Any
     purchase order, click-through, or other terms provided by Recipient are
     rejected and have no effect. Recipient agrees that this Agreement is
     accepted, and has the same force and effect as a manual signature, upon
     Recipient’s access to or use of the Feed. The words “include,” “includes,”
     and “including” are deemed to be followed by “without limitation.”
